## Workspace — one chain per package

Each package has its own hexagon, its own chain and its own `AGENTS.md` with its
graph and touch-area table. Route a request by path using the table in
`{{MEMORY_FILE}}`, then dispatch that package's agents (`<prefix>-<agent>`).

A change that crosses packages is **two chains, sequenced by the shared
contract** — never one chain. Run the chain of the package that owns the
contract first, to `STATUS: done` through verify; then dispatch the consuming
package's chain with the finished contract in its prompts.

## No meta-orchestrator subagent

There is no subagent that dispatches the others. A subagent that dispatches
subagents would collapse the root's turn-level parallelism and collapse multiple
receipts into one opaque summary — the root agent always walks the graph itself,
turn by turn, whether the change is small or a full vertical slice.
